-- title:
--   Local universal property after flat base change, assuming charts
-- statement:
--   The ambient data are the following. A domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (the hypothesis `hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi \in \mathcal O$, and the hypothesis `hcomplete` that $\mathcal O$ is adically complete for the ideal $(\pi)$. A tower of schemes $X_n$ ($n \in \mathbb N$) with structure morphisms $xb_n : X_n \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and transition morphisms $xt_n : X_n \to X_{n+1}$, such that (`hcart`) each square formed by $xt_n$, $xb_n$, $xb_{n+1}$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the reduction $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+2} \to \mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ is cartesian, each $xb_n$ is proper (`hproper`) and flat (`hflat`), and (`haff`) every finite subset of $X_n$ is contained in an affine open of $X_n$. A finite group $G$ acts through homomorphisms $a_n : G \to \operatorname{Aut}(X_n)$ compatibly with the structure morphisms (`ha_over`: $xb_n \circ a_n(g) = xb_n$) and with the transitions (`ha_xt`: $a_{n+1}(g) \circ xt_n = xt_n \circ a_n(g)$). Finally $D$ is a `TowerQuotientDatum` for these data: it consists of schemes $D.Y_n$ with structure morphisms $D.yb_n$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and transitions $D.yt_n$ whose squares over the reductions are cartesian, with each $D.yb_n$ proper and flat, together with morphisms $D.p_n : X_n \to D.Y_n$ over the base, commuting with the transitions, such that each square $(xt_n, D.p_n, D.p_{n+1}, D.yt_n)$ is cartesian, each $D.p_n$ is $G$-invariant, finite and surjective, each restriction $D.p_n \mid_U$ over an open $U \subseteq D.Y_n$ is an epimorphism, and $D$ carries the local universal property `univ_loc`: compatible $G$-invariant families of morphisms out of the $D.p_n$-preimages of a compatible family of opens of the $D.Y_n$ factor through those opens.
--
--   The base change is given by a flat $\mathcal O$-algebra $S$ ($\pi$ being written for its image $\operatorname{algebraMap}_{\mathcal O,S}(\pi)$ below), schemes $X'_n$ with structure morphisms $xb'_n : X'_n \to \operatorname{Spec}(S/\pi^{n+1})$, transitions $xt'_n$, actions $a'_n : G \to \operatorname{Aut}(X'_n)$ and morphisms $q_n : X'_n \to X_n$, subject to: `hq`, each square $(q_n, xb'_n, xb_n, \operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1} \to S/\pi^{n+1})$ is cartesian; `hcart'`, the squares of $xt'_n$ over the reductions $S/\pi^{n+2} \to S/\pi^{n+1}$ are cartesian; `hq_xt`, $q_{n+1} \circ xt'_n = xt_n \circ q_n$; `hq_a`, $q_n \circ a'_n(g) = a_n(g) \circ q_n$; and `ha'_over`, $xb'_n \circ a'_n(g) = xb'_n$.
--
--   The putative base-changed quotient is given abstractly: schemes $Y'_n$ with structure morphisms $yb'_n : Y'_n \to \operatorname{Spec}(S/\pi^{n+1})$, transitions $yt'_n$, morphisms $p'_n : X'_n \to Y'_n$ and $r_n : Y'_n \to D.Y_n$, subject to: `hbase`, each square $(r_n, yb'_n, D.yb_n, \operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1} \to S/\pi^{n+1})$ is cartesian; `hsq`, each square $(q_n, p'_n, D.p_n, r_n)$ is cartesian; `hyt'r`, $r_{n+1} \circ yt'_n = D.yt_n \circ r_n$; `hyt'b`, $yb'_{n+1} \circ yt'_n$ equals $yb'_n$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the reduction $S/\pi^{n+2} \to S/\pi^{n+1}$; `hp'_over`, $yb'_n \circ p'_n = xb'_n$; `hp'_inv`, $p'_n \circ a'_n(g) = p'_n$; and `hp'_xt`, $p'_{n+1} \circ xt'_n = yt'_n \circ p'_n$.
--
--   Two further hypotheses are imposed. The hypothesis `hP` asserts, for every $n$: the map of topological spaces underlying $p'_n$ is surjective and closed; any two points of $X'_n$ with the same image under $p'_n$ lie in one $G$-orbit for the action of the $a'_n(g)$; and every open $O \subseteq X'_n$ with $a'_n(g)^{-1}O = O$ for all $g \in G$ is of the form $p'^{-1}_n U'$ for some open $U' \subseteq Y'_n$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hchart` is a chart condition. For every family of opens $V_n \subseteq D.Y_n$ which are affine (`hVa`) and compatible, $D.yt_n^{-1}V_{n+1} = V_n$ (`hV`), it requires the existence of a ring $R$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure and a $G$-action by ring automorphisms commuting with the $\mathcal O$-action, such that $R$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, the image of $\pi$ is a non-zero-divisor on $R$, and $R/\pi R$ is of finite type over $\mathcal O$; and of isomorphisms of rings $\mathrm{lvl}_n : R/\pi^{n+1} \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } \Gamma(X_n, D.p_n^{-1}V_n)$ and $\mu_n : R^G/\pi^{n+1} \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } \Gamma(D.Y_n, V_n)$, where $R^G$ denotes the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $G$-fixed points, subject to six compatibilities: $\mathrm{lvl}$ intertwines the reduction maps of $R$ with the maps induced by $xt_n$ on sections; $\mathrm{lvl}_n$ intertwines the action of $g$ on $R$ with the map induced by $a_n(g^{-1})$; $\mathrm{lvl}_n$ sends the image of $o \in \mathcal O$ to the pullback along $xb_n$ of the global section $o \bmod \pi^{n+1}$ of $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$; $\mu$ is compatible with the maps induced by $D.yt_n$; $\mu_n$ followed by the map induced by $D.p_n$ agrees with $\mathrm{lvl}_n$ on $R^G \subseteq R$; and $\mu_n$ sends the image of $o \in \mathcal O$ to the pullback along $D.yb_n$ of $o \bmod \pi^{n+1}$.
--
--   In addition, `hchart` requires that for every $b \in R^G \otimes_{\mathcal O} S$ there are additive maps $\varphi_n : R^G \otimes_{\mathcal O} S \to \Gamma(Y'_n, r_n^{-1}V_n)$ with $\varphi_n(x \otimes s)$ equal to the product of the pullback along $r_n$ of $\mu_n(x \bmod \pi^{n+1})$ with the pullback along $yb'_n$ of the global section $s \bmod \pi^{n+1}$, each $\varphi_n$ surjective; that the basic opens are compatible, $yt'^{-1}_n\bigl(D(\varphi_{n+1}b)\bigr) = D(\varphi_n b)$ (this identity being named `hV'`); and that there is a primed chart ring $R'$, an $S$-algebra with a $G$-action by ring automorphisms commuting with the $S$-action, such that $R'$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that image is a non-zero-divisor on $R'$, the fixed subalgebra $R'^G$ is likewise adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, and there are ring isomorphisms $\mathrm{lvl}'_n : R'/\pi^{n+1} \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } \Gamma\bigl(X'_n, p'^{-1}_n D(\varphi_n b)\bigr)$ and $\mu'_n : R'^G/\pi^{n+1} \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } \Gamma\bigl(Y'_n, D(\varphi_n b)\bigr)$ satisfying the six analogous compatibilities: $\mathrm{lvl}'$ with the maps induced by $xt'_n$, with the maps induced by $a'_n(g^{-1})$ and the $G$-action on $R'$, and with the structure morphisms $xb'_n$ on images of elements of $S$; and $\mu'$ with the maps induced by $yt'_n$, with $\mathrm{lvl}'$ via the maps induced by $p'_n$, and with $yb'_n$ on images of elements of $S$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the local universal property for $(Y', p')$: for every scheme $T$, every family of opens $U_n \subseteq Y'_n$ with $yt'^{-1}_n U_{n+1} = U_n$ (the hypothesis `hU`), and every family of morphisms $u_n : p'^{-1}_n U_n \to T$ from the open subschemes $p'^{-1}_n U_n$, such that $u_n$ is invariant, $u_n \circ (a'_n(g) \text{ restricted to } p'^{-1}_n U_n \to p'^{-1}_n U_n) = u_n$ for all $n$ and all $g \in G$, and compatible, $u_{n+1} \circ (xt'_n \text{ restricted to } p'^{-1}_n U_n \to p'^{-1}_{n+1}U_{n+1}) = u_n$ for all $n$, there exists a family of morphisms $v_n : U_n \to T$ with $u_n$ equal to the restriction $p'_n \mid_{U_n} : p'^{-1}_n U_n \to U_n$ followed by $v_n$, for every $n$. No compatibility of the $v_n$ with the transitions $yt'_n$ is asserted.
--
--   This is the geometric half of the statement that the local universal property of a tower quotient datum survives flat base change: it derives the factorisation property `univ_loc` for the base-changed data $(Y', p')$ from the topological and orbit hypotheses on the $p'_n$ together with the existence of chart rings on compatible systems of affine opens. It is the input used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.univ_loc_of_isPullback_of_flat`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.univ_loc_of_isPullback_of_flat), where the charts are produced from the unprimed datum, and it relies on the flatness statements [`AlgebraicGeometry.epi_morphismRestrict_of_isPullback_of_flat`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.epi_morphismRestrict_of_isPullback_of_flat), [`AlgebraicGeometry.isAffineOpen_of_isAffineOpen_preimage_of_isPullback_of_flat`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.isAffineOpen_of_isAffineOpen_preimage_of_isPullback_of_flat) and [`AlgebraicGeometry.flat_specMap_quotientMap_pow_of_flat`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.flat_specMap_quotientMap_pow_of_flat).
